### *Part 1: Analyzing Complex Code*

*1. Repository Pattern - Why?*
Repository = middle layer between DB and business logic. Instead of `db.execute(select(User).where(...))` scattered in routes, you put it in `UserRepository.get_by_username()`.

Why: If tomorrow you switch SQLAlchemy to Mongo, you only change Repository, not 20 routes. Also testable - mock Repository, not DB. Generic `Repository[T]` means one base class handles `get_by_id`, `list` for ANY model - User, Post, Comment reuse same code.

*2. Generic Purpose*
`T = TypeVar('T', bound=Base)` = placeholder for model type. `Repository[User]` means `T` becomes `User`, so `get_by_id -> Optional[User]` type-checked. Without Generic you'd duplicate same CRUD for each model or lose type hints (return Any). Makes code maintainable: add new model = `class PostRepo(Repository[Post]): pass` gets all methods typed for free.[T]

*3. Dependency Injection Layers in this app:*
Layer 1 - Infrastructure: get_db() -> yields AsyncSession, handles open/close
Layer 2 - Data Access: UserRepository(User) uses db from Layer 1
Layer 3 - Business: UserService(repository) uses repo, has auth logic
Layer 4 - Auth: get_current_user(token + db) -> decodes JWT, calls repo to get User
Layer 5 - Endpoint: list_users(db + current_user) -> needs both DB and auth

FastAPI resolves bottom-up: request comes -> oauth2_scheme extracts token -> get_db creates session -> get_current_user uses both -> route gets final User object.
DI benefit: Route doesn't know how to create DB or verify JWT, just asks "give me current_user". Test? Override `get_db` with fake session.

*4. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)*
@requires_role("admin") # decorator factory
async def list_users(..., current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user))
Flow: decorator creates wrapper that injects `current_user` via Depends. Inside wrapper checks `is_superuser`. If not, 403. If yes, calls original function. Problem in this code: double injection - decorator AND route both request `current_user` - redundant but works. Better: decorator should handle injection alone.

